---
import resolution from '../../public/demo/interview-20261111/resolution.json';
const key = resolution.evidence.keys.find(key => key.id === 'did:web:did.is#key-1');
const lookupTime = resolution.observedAt.replace('T', ' ').replace('Z', ' UTC');
---
<section class="interview-demo not-content" data-interview-demo aria-label="Three questions about verifiable evidence">
  <div class="tour-heading">
    <span class="tour-eyebrow">A hands-on technical walkthrough</span>
    <p>Three questions about verifiable evidence.</p>
    <span class="tour-intro">Check a message, inspect a relation, then test the limits of a delegation. Start with a working case and change one condition.</span>
  </div>
  <nav class="chapter-navigation" aria-label="Walkthrough chapters">
    <ol>
      <li><button type="button" data-chapter="source" aria-controls="interview-source" aria-current="step"><span class="chapter-number">1</span><span><strong>Check the source</strong><small>Who signed it?</small></span></button></li>
      <li><button type="button" data-chapter="evidence" aria-controls="interview-evidence"><span class="chapter-number">2</span><span><strong>Inspect the evidence</strong><small>Why does the link count?</small></span></button></li>
      <li><button type="button" data-chapter="delegation" aria-controls="interview-delegation"><span class="chapter-number">3</span><span><strong>Check the limits</strong><small>What was delegated?</small></span></button></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <section id="interview-source" data-chapter-panel="source" class="chapter-panel" aria-labelledby="interview-source-title">
    <div class="chapter-heading">
      <span class="tour-eyebrow">Question 1 · source and exact words</span>
      <h2 id="interview-source-title" data-chapter-heading tabindex="-1">Who signed these exact words?</h2>
      <p>Start with <strong>Original statement</strong>. Then choose <strong>Different signer</strong>: its signature is real, but is it the source you expected?</p>
    </div>
    <details class="lookup-context">
      <summary>How does this identifier lead to a key?</summary>
      <div class="lookup-path"><code>{resolution.did}</code><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Website’s DID document</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><code>#key-1</code></div>
      <p><code>did:web</code> identifies an HTTPS document location. The saved lookup found the document at <code>{resolution.evidence.source.url}</code> and the key listed for <code>assertionMethod</code> — signing statements.</p>
      <p class="fine-print">Recorded lookup: {lookupTime}. Key type: {key?.curve}. This separate lookup is context, not evidence that the archived statement used a current key. <a href="/demo/interview-20261111/resolution.json">Inspect its original response</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <slot />
    <p class="chapter-takeaway"><span>Takeaway</span> A valid signature, the source you expected, and a valid date window are three separate checks.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="interview-evidence" data-chapter-panel="evidence" class="chapter-panel" aria-labelledby="interview-evidence-title" hidden>
    <div class="chapter-heading">
      <span class="tour-eyebrow">Question 2 · evidence behind a relation</span>
      <h2 id="interview-evidence-title" data-chapter-heading tabindex="-1">Why does this link count as evidence?</h2>
      <p>A visible link is not automatically a verified link. <strong>Choose a relationship</strong> to see what the saved lookup actually established.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="evidence-map">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 760 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="interview-map-title interview-map-desc">
        <title id="interview-map-title">Three selected relationships from one recorded DID lookup</title>
        <desc id="interview-map-desc">Website serves document; document lists signing key; key signs a domain-link proof. Select a relationship below to inspect its evidence. This is not a chain of trust.</desc>
        <defs><marker id="interview-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" /></marker></defs>
        <g class="map-links" fill="none" marker-end="url(#interview-arrow)">
          <path data-graph-line="served" d="M146 68H206" />
          <path data-graph-line="listed" d="M348 68H408" />
          <path data-graph-line="signed" d="M550 68H610" />
        </g>
        <g class="map-node"><rect x="4" y="30" width="142" height="76" rx="10"/><text x="75" y="61">Website</text><text x="75" y="83" class="map-sub">did.is</text></g>
        <g class="map-node"><rect x="206" y="30" width="142" height="76" rx="10"/><text x="277" y="61">DID document</text><text x="277" y="83" class="map-sub">Public declarations</text></g>
        <g class="map-node"><rect x="408" y="30" width="142" height="76" rx="10"/><text x="479" y="61">Signing key</text><text x="479" y="83" class="map-sub">#key-1</text></g>
        <g class="map-node"><rect x="610" y="30" width="142" height="76" rx="10"/><text x="681" y="61">Domain-link proof</text><text x="681" y="83" class="map-sub">One signed credential</text></g>
        <g class="map-labels"><text x="176" y="25">1</text><text x="378" y="25">2</text><text x="580" y="25">3</text></g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>A small projection of one recorded result — not a chain of trust or a complete network.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="relation-choices" role="group" aria-label="Choose a recorded relationship">
      <button type="button" data-relation="served" aria-pressed="false"><span class="choice-index">1</span><strong>Website → document</strong><span>Was it fetched?</span><small data-relation-state="served">Not loaded</small></button>
      <button type="button" data-relation="listed" aria-pressed="true"><span class="choice-index">2</span><strong>Document → key</strong><span>Was it listed?</span><small data-relation-state="listed">Not loaded</small></button>
      <button type="button" data-relation="signed" aria-pressed="false"><span class="choice-index">3</span><strong>Key → link proof</strong><span>Was its signature checked?</span><small data-relation-state="signed">Not loaded</small></button>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-result" data-graph-result data-tone="unknown" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" aria-busy="false">
      <div class="result-top"><span class="recorded-label">Recorded DID.is API result</span><strong class="result-state" data-graph-state>Not checked</strong></div>
      <h3 data-graph-headline>Choose a relationship to inspect.</h3>
      <p class="result-description" data-graph-summary>No positive conclusion has been made.</p>
      <div class="result-boundary"><strong>What this does not establish</strong><p data-graph-boundary>The graph explains the evidence. It does not create another proof.</p></div>
      <dl class="record-metadata"><div><dt>Source</dt><dd data-graph-source>Not established</dd></div><div><dt>Observed at</dt><dd data-graph-time>Not established</dd></div></dl>
    </div>
    <details class="technical-record"><summary>Inspect this relation’s original evidence</summary><p>The check method and evidence references below belong to this exact captured response, not a new verification.</p><pre data-graph-raw>No relation selected.</pre><p><a href="/demo/interview-20261111/graph.json">Full recorded Graph response</a> · <a href="/demo/interview-20261111/provenance.json">Capture details and file hashes</a></p></details>
    <p class="chapter-takeaway"><span>Takeaway</span> “Declared”, “observed” and “verified” answer different questions. Open the evidence before relying on a label.</p>
    <a class="guide-link" href="/app/evidence-graph/">Explore the full evidence Graph →</a>
  </section>

  <section id="interview-delegation" data-chapter-panel="delegation" class="chapter-panel" aria-labelledby="interview-delegation-title" hidden>
    <div class="chapter-heading">
      <span class="tour-eyebrow">Question 3 · the limits of a delegation</span>
      <h2 id="interview-delegation-title" data-chapter-heading tabindex="-1">Can a delegate go beyond its limits?</h2>
      <p>The demo owner delegates a limited grant to a helper, then a reader. <strong>Start within the limits</strong>, then change one condition.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="delegation-map" aria-label="Illustration of the three demo roles, not verified legal identities"><div><span class="actor-symbol" aria-hidden="true">A</span><strong>Demo owner</strong><small>Starts the signed chain</small></div><span class="role-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="actor-symbol" aria-hidden="true">B</span><strong>Helper</strong><small>Delegates within its grant</small></div><span class="role-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="actor-symbol" aria-hidden="true">C</span><strong>Reader</strong><small>Requests an action</small></div></div>
    <p class="map-caption"><strong>Separate recorded example:</strong> three disposable <code>did:key</code> identities, not the website’s signing key. The application chooses the starting owner to trust.</p>
    <div class="delegation-choices" role="group" aria-label="Choose one delegation condition">
      <button type="button" data-delegation-case="read" aria-pressed="true"><strong>Within the limits</strong><span>Read · expected owner</span></button>
      <button type="button" data-delegation-case="wrong-root" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Different expected owner</strong><span>Same chain · change the root</span></button>
      <button type="button" data-delegation-case="outside-scope" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Ask to write instead</strong><span>Same chain · different action</span></button>
      <button type="button" data-delegation-case="widened-child" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Delegate too much</strong><span>Genuine signature · wider claim</span></button>
    </div>
    <p class="changed-condition" data-delegation-change>No change — start with the read request.</p>
    <div class="evidence-result" data-delegation-result data-tone="unknown" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" aria-busy="false">
      <div class="result-top"><span class="recorded-label">Recorded verification · not current permission</span><strong class="result-state" data-delegation-decision>Not checked</strong></div>
      <h3 data-delegation-headline>Select a recorded check.</h3>
      <p class="result-description" data-delegation-explanation>This page does not approve or execute a task.</p>
      <dl class="request-summary"><div><dt>Requested capability</dt><dd><code data-delegation-tool>Not established</code></dd></div><div><dt>Recorded at</dt><dd data-delegation-time>Not established</dd></div><div><dt>Chain deadline in the record</dt><dd data-delegation-expiry>Not established</dd></div></dl>
      <ol class="delegation-checks" aria-label="Separate checks reported by the recorded verification">
        {['Signatures', 'Expected owner', 'Parent limits', 'Requested action', 'Dates at capture'].map(label => <li data-delegation-check data-status="unknown"><strong data-check-label>{label}</strong><span data-check-text>Not established</span></li>)}
      </ol>
    </div>
    <p class="no-execution"><strong>Verification only.</strong> These are recorded answers from the real verifier, not a new browser verification or a current grant. No action runs. The receipt format is DID.is Delegation Receipt v1 (experimental).</p>
    <details class="technical-record"><summary>Inspect the exact request and recorded answer</summary><p>Role illustration → actual recorded DID:</p><pre data-delegation-principals>Not established</pre><p>Application-selected trusted root(s):</p><pre class="root-value" data-delegation-root>Not established</pre><p>Receipt SHA-256 digests are compared with the captured per-link digests to bind the displayed request to its recorded answer. This is a consistency check, not new signature verification or a trusted timestamp.</p><p>Different-root, leaf-scope and parent-attenuation failures are separate cases. A modified payload with an old signature would only demonstrate a signature failure.</p><pre data-delegation-raw>No recorded case selected.</pre><p>The dates above describe the captured verifier’s time profile, not execution-time enforcement. <a href="/demo/interview-20261111/delegation.json">Download the public inputs and captured answers</a> · <a href="/reference/delegation-receipts/">Receipt format</a></p></details>
    <p class="chapter-takeaway"><span>Takeaway</span> Correct signatures do not replace the expected authority, parent limits or the requested action’s scope.</p>
    <a class="guide-link" href="/app/delegation/">Open the receipt inspector guide →</a>
  </section>

  <footer class="tour-footer"><button type="button" data-chapter-prev disabled>← Previous</button><span data-chapter-progress aria-live="polite">Chapter 1 of 3</span><button type="button" data-chapter-next><span data-chapter-next-label>Next: inspect the evidence</span> →</button></footer>
  <noscript><p>JavaScript is required for the interactive checks. The <a href="/demo/official-source-20261103/bundle.json">public statement bundle</a>, <a href="/demo/interview-20261111/graph.json">recorded Graph</a> and <a href="/demo/interview-20261111/delegation.json">delegation records</a> remain available for inspection.</p></noscript>
</section>
<script>
  import { initializeInterviewDemo } from '../lib/interviewDemo.mjs';
  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-interview-demo]')) initializeInterviewDemo(root);
</script>
<style>
